                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Unfortunately, [i]Angry Toad Studios[/i] (the developer), no longer exists. So there is that. I put that out there because I would like to know when I'm buying a product that is essentially 'dead' as far as possible future updates or serious support.\n---\n\n[b]With that being said, [i]The Depths of Tolagal[/i] is a well done logical-puzzle-esque roguelike in the same vein as [i]Space Grunts[/i].[/b] It's all about understanding how enemies move - how they are going to move, and how you are going to get in there and get the kill without being hit.\n\n[b]For five bucks, it's a fun little coffee-break roguelike.[/b] It can be played entirely from the keyboard or mouse, which I appreciate. \n\n[b]Pros:[/b]\n+What I am really recommending with this one is the fun mechanic - most everything else is ho-hum\n+Full keyboard or mouse support\n+It's cheap\n+It's a true roguelike\n\n[b]Cons:[/b]\n-Story is forgetable\n-Weapons are run-of-the-mill standard deals\n-Not really any design risks; some people [i]love[/i] the leveling up process with 'talents', but it's all been done before\n\n[b]Fun distraction in small bursts.[/b]",
